<!-- @after 7. Deep Dive: Read/Write Path with Two Tiers (15 min) :: animation -->
### Follow one entry through both tiers

<figure class="stepper" data-illustrated><span class="stepper-title">Write now, flush later, expire on read</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="viz-grid" data-cols="3"><div class="node" data-el="caller" data-art="code" data-art-role="client"><strong>Caller</strong><small data-text="callerV">Cache&lt;K, V&gt;</small></div><div class="node" data-el="memory" data-art="memory" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Memory tier</strong><small data-text="memoryV">LRU, bounded</small></div><div class="node" data-el="writer" data-art="worker" data-art-role="queue"><strong>Disk queue</strong><small data-text="writerV">idle</small></div></div><div class="viz-grid" data-cols="3"><div class="node" data-el="tmp" data-art="document" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Temporary file</strong><small data-text="tmpV">none</small></div><div class="node" data-el="entry" data-art="database" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Disk entry</strong><small data-text="entryV">none</small></div></div><div class="node is-key" data-el="event" data-art="signal" data-art-role="runtime"><strong>What happens</strong><small data-text="eventV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
