  },
  {
    "label": "Atomic write to disk",
    "caption": "The serialized bytes go to a .tmp file, fsync flushes them, and rename puts the file in place. A crash before the rename leaves any earlier entry untouched. One consumer runs disk operations in queue order, one at a time, and the byte budget is checked after each write.",
