      "to": "entry",
      "kind": "page",
      "label": "rename"
    }
  },
  {
    "label": "A memory hit, if still fresh",
    "caption": "get() checks memory first. An entry that hasn’t expired returns straight away and counts as a hit. An expired one is removed, and the read moves on to disk.",
    "state": {
      "caller": "active",
      "memory": "active",
      "tmp": "done"
    },
    "text": {
      "memoryV": "hit: not expired",
      "eventV": "expiry is checked on every read"
    }
  },
  {
    "label": "A cold read promotes",
    "caption": "After a restart or an eviction, memory misses. The disk entry is still fresh, so it’s deserialized and returned, and goes back in memory with its original expiresAt unless a put or invalidate ran meanwhile. Its age doesn’t reset.",
